From b70ce0eb96b08e7fab7762d4425d47d2b929b2f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:53:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(state): a host wake does not hand a live
 holder's lapsed turn lease to the first waiter

On laptop-1 (2026-11-14 08:29:34 PST) a TUI turn held chat 20000101_030000_000001's turn lease, the Mac
slept ~7 min, the 300 s wall-clock TTL ran out during the sleep, and on the DarkWake the gateway's notice
turn reclaimed the row before the holder's 60 s refresher tick could renew it. The holder's finished reply
was then refused ('another Hermes process took over this session'); chat 20000101_030000_000002 lost its
turn the same way in the same second.

Acquisition (SessionDB.try_acquire_session_turn_lease and the runtime worker's turn.acquire) now keeps an
expired row whose holder is not provably dead for WAKE_GRACE_SECONDS (90) of awake time after this
process first sees a host suspend (suspend-inclusive clock minus time.monotonic grows). The holder's
_renew_after_lapse tick lands inside that grace; a holder that never renews is reclaimed after it, a dead
holder at once. Hosts without a suspend (Linux servers, CI) see no change.

Self-heal t_01a1dae544d34841 (gateway-34796400a6).
